      ":question/problem": "Express $\\frac{2}{3}\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\frac{2}{3}\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)$ as a single trigonometric ratio.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Collect the common factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\frac{2}{3}\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\frac{2}{3}\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the cosine double-angle formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos^2 x-\\sin^2 x=\\cos(2x)\n$$\n\nSubstitute $x=31^\\circ$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)&=\\cos\\left(2\\cdot 31^\\circ\\right)\\\\&=\\cos\\left(62^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKeep the outside factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\cos^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)-\\sin^2\\left(31^\\circ\\right)\\right)&=\\frac{2}{3}\\cos\\left(62^\\circ\\right)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
